  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final text sets 7% (not the 5% benchmark) as the permanent S2 limit, with no sales stop and no bound on regulator-set remediation, and gives customers numeric per-model rates while keeping public reporting aggregated; this protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 keeps 8/100k only as a notification and corrective-action trigger with recall left to regulator discretion, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S3 (24 months for new units, 6-year retrofit) and S4 (36-month suppression) are the other main concessions, and S1 (24-hour reporting of all incidents) is the strongest section."
 },
